From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] usb-host: Darwin session accounting and native lease bridge

What: serialize public-session reservations, retain callback lifetimes and add
six exact-receipt QMP handlers with an internal one-shot native HID ticket.
Revoke disables submits, asynchronously cancels/drains/closes, then permits
exact guard release and generation thaw. Unknown cleanup remains frozen.
Why: empty queues and device_del are not native-close or ownership receipts.
Upstream: OmacVM PR427; local Darwin integration, not submitted to QEMU.
Ordinary transport and official libusb unchanged; no extra context or producer.
Handle-lifetime synchronous fences, checked cleanup, QOM reentrancy and explicit
native-neverstarted cleanup ACK. Idle never-leased session refs are reclaimed.
Included in the normal runtime recipe; the VM's Vendor HID switch stays OFF
by default. See Tests/coexistence/README.md for portable checks and limits.
Applies after qemu-usb-host-busy-device.patch at QEMU c3d48b7d1e89604920e5b81b91140c2ad39a1943.
Test: run-candidate.py, run-dispatch.py, actual QMP/native API fixtures and
whole-unit actual-core inert lifecycle checks. No hardware is run by these tests.

